  "description": "The androidtester gantry in miniature, two-axis, deck-and-gantry separated: the android_phone lies on the deck (the phone plate on the beam centre), and an ELEVATED X rail rides above it on stacked corner-bracket standoffs. The Y stage hangs from the elevated X carriage: a Y rail (yaw-90) with a guided T8 nut driven by a sideways T8 leadscrew (8 mm/rev); the touch_finger hangs from the guided nut, its plunger descending to tap the glass. Drive motor_left/right for X, y_leadscrew for Y; tap_at positions both axes and taps.",
